# Data Structure Complexity Cheat Sheet

Notation: n = number of elements, L = key/string length, V = vertices, E = edges, k = result size / hash count, B = B-tree branching factor.
Best and worst case are separate columns; average case is mentioned in Notes where it differs a lot (hash, BST, skip list).
"amortized" = averaged over a sequence of operations (one op can be slower, e.g. a resize).

---

## 1. Time and space complexity matrix

How to read it:

- Insert / Delete = add or remove one element the normal way for that structure (stack push / pop, queue enqueue / dequeue, heap extract top, hash and tree by key).
- Search = find by value or key. Update = change the value of an existing element found by key / value (a key change in an ordered structure = delete + insert).
- n/a = not supported. `*` = amortized.

| Data structure | Insert best | Insert worst | Search best | Search worst | Delete best | Delete worst | Update best | Update worst | Space | Notes |
|------------------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|--------|----------------------------------------|
| **Linear** | | | | | | | | | | |
| Array (fixed) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(n) | End is O(1); front / middle shifts O(n). Index read / update O(1) |
| Dynamic array | O(1)* | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(n) | Append amortized O(1), resize O(n). Index read / update O(1) |
| Sorted array | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(log n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(n) | Binary search O(log n); insert / delete shift O(n) |
| Singly linked list | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(n) | Head O(1); tail without tail pointer, or by value O(n) |
| Doubly linked list | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(n) | O(1) for any node already held; O(n) to find by value |
| Stack | O(1) | O(1) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(1) | O(1) | O(n) | O(n) | Push / pop / peek top O(1); arbitrary element O(n) |
| Queue | O(1) | O(1) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(1) | O(1) | O(n) | O(n) | Enqueue / dequeue / peek front O(1) |
| Deque | O(1) | O(1) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(1) | O(1) | O(n) | O(n) | O(1) at both ends; middle O(n) |
| **Hash based** | | | | | | | | | | |
| Hash map / hash set | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) | O(n) | O(n) | Avg O(1). Worst O(n) on collisions or resize (O(log n) with Java 8+ tree buckets) |
| Bloom filter | O(k) | O(k) | O(k) | O(k) | n/a | n/a | n/a | n/a | O(m) bits | False positives possible, no false negatives; counting variant can delete |
